Z||000003||Jay||06-06-2001||07:56 AM||||Will, wouldn't that be the best place to start?  I mean if all the unnecessary stuff is already gone, how difficult would it be to modify what is there for a car.  i would imagine that the program would be much simpler to hack.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||06-06-2001||12:49 PM||||If you have the skills, and if the program is capable of interpreting a bigger map.<P>But you might as well go with an aftermarket ECM if you do that. All the extraneous junk is already gone from a Haltech, it's ready to be programmed, and you wouldn't have to do any pioneering work with it.<P>What would you use to control your transmission if you did this?<P>Neither is even close to being as sophisitcated as a GM ECM, however.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jay||06-06-2001||04:51 PM||||Well then the question is how much is a Haltech?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||06-06-2001||06:58 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.haltech.com" TARGET=_blank>www.haltech.com</A> <P>1FST2M6 would know more.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com" TARGET=_blank>www.chrfab.com</A>  sells electromotive and holley units as well. Both of which appear to be reasonably easy to install.||||reg||1
